uilder already found and fixed, confirmed here to be a genuine catalog-level gap, not year-specific): THEA 270 (Semester 5) requires ALL of THEA 201W, THEA 251, AND THEA 252 per the real course catalog -- THEA 251 is already scheduled (Semester 4) but neither THEA 201W nor THEA 252 appears anywhere in the bulletin's own Suggested Academic Plan table for Stage Management (confirmed by direct inspection: this is a real omission in Penn State's own advising plan, not a scraper artifact). Fixed identically to 2026: Semester 4 replaces 2 of its 3 raw 'General Education Course' slots with explicit THEA 252 (1cr) and THEA 201W (3cr) items, dropping Semester 4's target from the bulletin's own printed 15 to 13 (net -2cr, same trade 2026 made). self-verified: planner_engine.build_full_plan(start_year=2023, today=2023-07-01) now completes in 7 terms with zero warnings and goal met.",
